00:23:15.360 --> 00:23:19.820
Um, but now if you lightly touch a wall, you will just explode.

00:23:20.140 --> 00:23:23.140
Um, which is odd considering how slow you move.

00:23:23.620 --> 00:23:25.660
Um, yeah, just the same complaints.

00:23:26.140 --> 00:23:29.400
Yeah, I would say, too, especially in the later levels, it's surprising.

00:23:30.220 --> 00:23:33.120
That there's so many enemies on the screen at once.

00:23:33.280 --> 00:23:40.320
I think they thought that was the way to up the challenge without necessarily testing, like, how those enemies shoot.

00:23:40.540 --> 00:23:45.540
Because the way that they shoot, you know, very few enemies shoot at you, like, head on, right?

00:23:45.640 --> 00:23:50.680
Like, just they shoot straight down and you just have to line up with them and dodge their shot and shoot their shot.

00:23:50.760 --> 00:23:56.040
Most of these enemies shoot diagonally in, in the, in whatever which way they feel like.

00:23:56.040 --> 00:24:05.000
Like, so you wind up getting too many enemies of that and then it's, like, an entire, like, zone has, of the screen has been, like, cornered off for you.

00:24:05.000 --> 00:24:14.020
And if you just happen to be unluckily in that area when those enemies come in, you might just be in the line of fire with no way out.

00:24:14.020 --> 00:24:17.400
Uh, which is unfortunate because it's easier.

00:24:17.400 --> 00:24:28.220
It's easier, and this is true of a lot of video games, it's easier when watching, uh, somebody who is beating the game, like, watching a playthrough after the fact and, and seeing what needs to be done.

00:24:28.220 --> 00:24:37.000
